; open-textbook.org — a BIND zone file for Cloudflare's "Import DNS records".
;
; Dashboard: DNS → Records → Import and Export → Import DNS records. Upload this
; file. It ADDS the records below; it does not touch the apex records that the
; Worker's custom domain owns, because nothing here names the apex with an
; A/AAAA/CNAME.
;
; Before importing: check the "Proxy imported DNS records" box STAYS TICKED. The
; redirect in the second block only works for a proxied hostname, and a redirect
; rule cannot fire for a name Cloudflare does not proxy. The cf_tags comment on
; the www record forces it either way, and takes precedence over the checkbox.
;
; See DEPLOY.md, "DNS: the www redirect".

$ORIGIN open-textbook.org.

; --- www: a redirect, not a copy ---------------------------------------------
; www has to RESOLVE and be PROXIED, or nothing can answer for it. It is not a
; second origin: the redirect rule returns 301 to the apex before any content is
; served. The address is therefore never contacted, and 100:: is the IPv6
; discard prefix (RFC 6666), which exists for exactly this purpose.
; cf_tags=cf-proxied:true wins over the import form's proxy setting.
www.open-textbook.org.  300  IN  AAAA  100::  ; cf_tags=cf-proxied:true

; --- mail: the domain neither sends nor receives ------------------------------
; A textbook has no reason to send mail, so SPF denies every sender and DMARC
; rejects on failure. Together they close the domain as a spoofing source, and
; an empty SPF record is the strongest form: "v=spf1 -all" means "no host may
; send as this domain". No rua: nobody is reading reports, and an address that
; nobody reads is worse than none.
open-textbook.org.       300  IN  TXT   "v=spf1 -all"
_dmarc.open-textbook.org.  300  IN  TXT   "v=DMARC1; p=reject"

; --- CAA: verify before enabling, then uncomment ------------------------------
; CAA restricts which certificate authorities may issue for this domain. It is
; real hardening and it has a delayed failure mode: if the list omits the CA
; Cloudflare actually uses, nothing breaks today and the certificate fails to
; RENEW weeks later. So it stays off until checked against Cloudflare's current
; list (SSL/TLS → Edge Certificates → CAA, or the certificate's issuer).
;
; These three are the CAs Cloudflare documents for custom domains. Note the
; pki.goog parameter, and that it must stay inside the quotes: a semicolon
; outside quotes starts a BIND comment.
; open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issue     "letsencrypt.org"
; open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issue     "pki.goog; cansignhttpexchanges=yes"
; open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issue     "ssl.com"
; open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issuewild  "letsencrypt.org"
; open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issuewild  "pki.goog; cansignhttpexchanges=yes"
; open-textbook.org.  300  IN  CAA  0 issuewild  "ssl.com"
